{"id":1,"explanation":"The nonce check in verify prevents a token whose nonce is already in seen from being accepted again. Removing it would allow replay attacks. #123 is an issue reference.","unsure":""}
{"id":2,"explanation":"Call ensure_key_salt before constructing KeyManager. If salt setup fails, abort startup rather than initializing the manager. There are no issue, file, or document references.","unsure":""}
{"id":3,"explanation":"Before allocating buf, topN must be no greater than maxSimpleTopN so the resulting slice stays at or below 1 MiB. There are no external references.","unsure":""}
{"id":4,"explanation":"When meta.abi_version is missing, abi must remain None; treating the missing value as the current ABI would be unsafe. #1784 is an issue reference.","unsure":""}
{"id":5,"explanation":"The drop-in written under /etc/tlp.d/ can be overridden by /etc/tlp.conf because TLP reads that file last. Both paths name configuration locations.","unsure":""}
{"id":6,"explanation":"This configuration requires TLP version 1.10 or later. _AC, _BAT, and _SAV name profile suffixes; the setting shown targets the battery profile. Leaving the AC setting unset preserves GNOME’s Performance toggle. There are no issue or document references.","unsure":""}
{"id":7,"explanation":"On a JsonException, this code deliberately returns null so the caller can log a warning. There are no external references.","unsure":""}
{"id":8,"explanation":"When AllowedTools restrictions are set, remove --dangerously-skip-permissions from the arguments because that flag bypasses --allowedTools. The comment applies to RemoveSkipPermissions(args); the named flags are command-line options.","unsure":""}
{"id":9,"explanation":"For the behavior of thunk_is_dead, consult the verdict table at the is_definitely_dead_code symbol in rust/xray-core/src/compiler/graph_preamble.rs. That path and symbol are a code reference.","unsure":""}
{"id":10,"explanation":"repos_skipped is currently set to zero; the planned work is to derive it from the domains-to-repos mapping. #874 is the tracking issue.","unsure":""}
{"id":11,"explanation":"index.regex_query(pattern) is expected to use a linear-time DFA without backtracking. The comment records the performance property developers should preserve. There are no external references.","unsure":""}
{"id":12,"explanation":"Keep the token-family table schema in this SQL definition synchronized with RefreshTokenSqliteBackend._ensure_schema in src/storage/refresh_token_backend.py. The path and method name identify the related code.","unsure":""}
{"id":13,"explanation":"MAX_BATCH is 500 because the vendor’s batch API accepts at most 500 items. doc:vendor-api#limits points to the vendor API documentation’s limits anchor.","unsure":""}
{"id":14,"explanation":"Keep these Status values aligned with STATUS_LABELS in web/src/status.ts. Reordering the iota constants would change what already-stored integer values mean. #88 is an issue reference; the path and STATUS_LABELS name identify the related code.","unsure":""}
{"id":15,"explanation":"The index must list tenant_id first and created_at second to match the orders_by_tenant query. orders_by_tenant names the related query; no file path or issue is given.","unsure":""}
{"id":16,"explanation":"FCount must never exceed the length of FItems, and Grow is responsible for preserving that condition as the list grows. These names refer to the list’s fields and growth operation.","unsure":""}
{"id":17,"explanation":"Flush before closing the sink: closing it drops _buf, so reversing these calls could lose buffered data. _flush and _buf name the relevant method and buffer.","unsure":""}
{"id":18,"explanation":"A path supplied by a request must be resolved under workspaceRoot, and paths using '..' to escape that root must be rejected. The shown line resolves and normalizes userPath; the comment also requires an escape check, which is not shown.","unsure":""}
{"id":19,"explanation":"Drain the ring before freeing buf. If buf is freed first, the interrupt handler could still use it, causing a use-after-free. #2201 is an issue reference.","unsure":""}
{"id":20,"explanation":"reserve(n) allocates capacity for items once; prior growth through push_back accounted for 40% of the measured profile. doc:perf-notes#ingest points to the ingest section of the performance notes.","unsure":""}
{"id":21,"explanation":"Keep HOLDLOCK on this SQL Server MERGE because concurrent upserts can race without it. doc:mssql-merge#concurrency points to the concurrency section of the cited documentation.","unsure":""}
{"id":22,"explanation":"The autonomous transaction is deliberate: it lets the audit row survive even if the calling transaction rolls back. There are no external references.","unsure":""}
{"id":23,"explanation":"This migration creates a replacement table because SQLite ALTER TABLE cannot directly drop the relevant constraints. doc:sqlite-alter#otheralter points to the cited SQLite ALTER TABLE documentation section.","unsure":"The snippet does not identify which constraints are being dropped."}
{"id":24,"explanation":"The loop polls every five seconds because NFS mounts do not emit the inotify events this code would need. The 5 in done.wait(5) is the polling interval in seconds.","unsure":""}
{"id":25,"explanation":"Keep the for...of loop when awaiting each job. Putting await inside forEach would let asynchronous errors escape the surrounding try/catch. The comment applies to the jobs iteration.","unsure":""}
{"id":26,"explanation":"The returned Vec<u8> frame must have length at most MAX_FRAME; read_frame’s decoder enforces this by rejecting larger frames. MAX_FRAME names the size limit.","unsure":""}
{"id":27,"explanation":"Register the shutdown hook before starting the pool so it is available to drain the pool on SIGTERM. addShutdownHook and pool.start() are the calls whose order matters.","unsure":""}
{"id":28,"explanation":"The retry policy is currently hard-coded in backoff; the planned change is to move it into configuration. internal/retry/policy.go:Default identifies the code location intended to read that configuration.","unsure":"The comment does not establish whether Default already reads configuration or describes the planned behavior."}
{"id":29,"explanation":"See issue #412 for the full matrix of transitions between LeaseState values such as Active, Released, and Stale.","unsure":""}
{"id":30,"explanation":"Pass the token through standard input, as --token-stdin does, instead of placing it in command-line arguments. Other users can see arguments through ps, exposing the token. TOKEN is the shell variable holding it.","unsure":""}
{"id":31,"explanation":"Create app_reader before granting it privileges. Migration 042 assumes the role already exists; 042 is a migration number, and app_reader is the database role.","unsure":""}
{"id":32,"explanation":"The Stripe webhook handler must be idempotent because Stripe may retry a webhook for three days. doc:stripe#webhook-retries points to the cited webhook retry documentation.","unsure":""}
{"id":33,"explanation":"Compare the signature and expected MAC with hmac.Equal, which uses a constant-time comparison. Using == could reveal information through timing differences. hmac.Equal is the required function.","unsure":""}
{"id":34,"explanation":"Build the graph once per index, at O(edges) cost, rather than rebuilding it for each query. CodeGraph::build is the operation this performance rule applies to.","unsure":""}
{"id":35,"explanation":"Changing TCustomerRec’s packed record layout would make existing saved .dat files incompatible. Bump FILE_VERSION when changing that layout; FILE_VERSION names the file-format version.","unsure":""}
{"id":36,"explanation":"Change MSG_MAX and MSG_MAX_WIRE together. proto/messages.h:MSG_MAX_WIRE identifies the related constant in the header file.","unsure":""}
{"id":37,"explanation":"handler assumes authMiddleware has run and has set session.userId to a non-null value. authMiddleware names the middleware that establishes this condition.","unsure":""}
{"id":38,"explanation":"The cache uses synchronization because its check-then-put sequence must be atomic. A ConcurrentHashMap alone would not make that multi-step sequence atomic. cache is the synchronized object.","unsure":""}
{"id":39,"explanation":"Validate a user-supplied repository alias against the registry before joining it into a path, to prevent unsafe path selection. validate_alias(raw) performs the shown validation. #1996 is an issue reference.","unsure":""}
{"id":40,"explanation":"Inserted Payment amounts must be nonnegative. Refunds are represented as separate rows with Kind equal to 'R', rather than as negative amounts. Amount and Kind are columns in the shown INSERT.","unsure":""}
{"id":41,"explanation":"Set stop_ before joining worker_. Otherwise the worker may never exit and join could block forever. These are the stop flag and worker being joined.","unsure":""}
{"id":42,"explanation":"The limiter is set in light of a GitHub API allowance of 5,000 requests per hour per token; one request every 720 milliseconds corresponds to that rate. doc:github-rest#rate-limits points to the cited rate-limits documentation.","unsure":""}
{"id":43,"explanation":"Stop the cidx service before installing its replacement binary. Replacing a running binary can fail with 'Text file busy'. The path /usr/local/bin/cidx is the binary being replaced.","unsure":""}
{"id":44,"explanation":"Do not share one _lease across jobs serving different users: its credentials could leak from one user’s job to another. #77 is an issue reference.","unsure":""}
{"id":45,"explanation":"Keep ids at 999 entries or fewer for this DELETE statement, because the comment treats 999 as SQLite’s bound-variable limit per statement. len(ids) is the number of values bound to the generated placeholders.","unsure":""}
{"id":46,"explanation":"If cgroup creation fails, warn and let the job continue. This is deliberate so a bad memory estimate does not abort the job. cgroup.create(limit) is the operation whose failure is handled.","unsure":""}
{"id":47,"explanation":"The /v1/jobs route is a legacy route scheduled for removal. #530 is the tracking issue; '/v1' is the route prefix.","unsure":""}
{"id":48,"explanation":"Consult the session-model section of ADR 007 for the reason sessions are per tab. doc:adr-007#session-model is the document anchor; the comment applies to SessionRegistry.","unsure":""}
{"id":49,"explanation":"This partial index targets active-lease lookups by indexing only rows where released_at IS NULL. The comment reports a 30× speedup for that lookup; credential_id is the indexed column.","unsure":""}
{"id":50,"explanation":"Keep EVENT_TYPES synchronized with EVENT_LABELS in web/src/events.ts and with docs/events.md. The first path and symbol identify related code; the second path identifies related documentation.","unsure":""}
